// Dev-server reverse proxy for the default (direct) serve mode.
//
// The frontend reads one service address itself, the service-locator address
// in src/assets/conf/chipster.yaml, and gets every other address from
// service-locator. That one address is relative, so that it works in both
// serve modes without editing the file, which means the dev server has to
// proxy it even in the direct mode. Everything else the browser requests
// directly from the service ports, using the absolute url-ext-* addresses
// service-locator hands out.
//
// Proxy mode uses proxy.conf.mjs instead, which has this same entry and the
// rest of the services too.
//
// No keep-alive agent here, unlike proxy.conf.mjs, so the responses of this
// one entry still say "Connection: close" and the dev server closes the
// connection of the browser after each of them. Nothing has gone wrong with a
// truncated response here, because the service list is a couple of kilobytes,
// and an agent is not a JSON value, so adding one would turn this file into
// JavaScript for a case that has never needed it. Should this mode ever
// truncate a response too, see the explanation in proxy.conf.mjs.
{
  "/service-locator": {
    "target": "http://localhost:8003",
    "pathRewrite": { "^/service-locator": "" }
  }
}
